@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Contract: Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a doc → `get(id)` returns deep-equal content
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` on existing id (current branch) throws
+- [ ] `get(id)` on missing id throws
+- [ ] `get(id)` on deleted id throws
+- [ ] `get(id)` returns a deep clone (mutating result doesn't affect store)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` deep clones input (mutating input after create doesn't affect store)
+- [ ] `update(id, content)` replaces content → `get(id)` reflects new content
+- [ ] `update(id, content)` on missing id throws
+- [ ] `delete(id)` removes doc → subsequent `get`/`update`/`delete` throw
+- [ ] `delete(id)` on missing id throws
+
+## Version History
+- [ ] `create` produces one version in `getHistory(id)`
+- [ ] each `update` appends a new version; `getHistory` returns oldest→newest
+- [ ] each version has unique `id`, a `timestamp`, and correct `content`
+- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns content of that specific version
+- [ ] `getVersion` with bad id/versionId throws
+
+## Branching
+- [ ] default branch is `"main"`; `getBranch()` returns it initially
+- [ ] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state
+- [ ] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from named branch instead
+- [ ] `createBranch` on duplicate name throws
+- [ ] `switchBranch(name)` changes `getBranch()` and active CRUD scope
+- [ ] `switchBranch` on unknown branch throws
+- [ ] `listBranches()` includes all created branches, `"main"` present initially
+- [ ] writes on one branch are invisible on another (isolation)
+- [ ] branch created from a branch inherits that branch's docs/history at fork time
+
+## Merge — no conflicts
+- [ ] merge with no changes on either side is a no-op, `applied: true`, empty conflicts
+- [ ] change only on source branch is auto-applied to current branch
+- [ ] change only on current branch: merge is no-op-equivalent (ours already has it), `applied: true`
+- [ ] same field changed identically on both sides → no conflict, value applied
+- [ ] different fields changed on each side → both changes merged, no conflict
+- [ ] nested/nested field changes on each side merge structurally (deep merge)
+- [ ] doc created only on source branch → appears in current branch after merge
+- [ ] doc deleted on source (unchanged on current) → deleted on current after merge
+- [ ] unrelated documents changed independently on each branch merge cleanly together
+- [ ] successful merge actually mutates current branch's documents/history
+
+## Merge — conflicts
+- [ ] same field changed to different values on both sides → conflict reported with correct path/base/ours/theirs
+- [ ] conflicting merge does NOT apply changes to current branch (state unchanged)
+- [ ] conflicting merge still returns full `merged` object with "ours" value at conflicted path
+- [ ] multiple conflicts across different documents/paths are all reported
+- [ ] `merge` result `applied` is `false` whenever `conflicts.length > 0`
+
+## Verification
+- All criteria above verified via `npm test` (vitest) in `tests/`.
+- `npm run build` (tsc) passes with no errors.
+- `npm run lint` passes with no errors.
